## WHAT SANDFLY IS

Sandfly is an agentless compromise and intrusion detection system for Linux. Key architectural facts:

  Architecture: Core server (REST API + PostgreSQL + web UI) + separate scanning nodes.
  Agentless: No software installed on protected hosts. Nodes connect via SSH, push ephemeral
             sandfly modules, collect forensic data, report back. Zero footprint on endpoints.
  Scanning: Server dispatches scan tasks to nodes. Nodes use SSH (with stored encrypted credentials
            or jump hosts) to reach protected Linux systems.
  Nodes: Can span multiple networks, cloud providers, and isolated segments.
         Each node contacts the server via the REST API.
  Jump hosts: Nodes can route through SSH bastion hosts to reach isolated networks.

  API version number is INDEPENDENT of the Sandfly product version.
  Current API version prefix: v4  (e.g. https://{{SANDFLY_HOST}}/v4/...)
  Latest product version: 5.6.0

