## NORMALIZED ALERT SCHEMA FOR GITOPS-ALERT-RESOLVER

When routing Sandfly alerts into your gitops-alert-resolver pipeline, normalize each result to:

  {
    "source":      "sandfly",
    "host_id":     "<sandfly_host_uuid>",
    "host_addr":   "<ip_or_hostname>",
    "alert_id":    "<sandfly_result_uuid>",
    "sandfly_name": "process_deleted",
    "severity":    4,
    "status":      "alert",
    "mitre_ids":   ["T1070.004"],
    "mitre_tactics": ["defense_evasion"],
    "key_data":    "/tmp/malware_binary",
    "type":        "process",
    "timestamp":   "2026-03-13T10:00:00Z",
    "forensics": {
      "process_name": "malware_binary",
      "pid":          13311,
      "sha256":       "<hash>",
      "cmdline":      "/tmp/malware_binary --connect c2.evil.com"
    },
    "tags":        ["tag:k3s-node", "tag:prod"]
  }

Redis deduplication key: sha256(source + host_id + sandfly_name + key_data + date(timestamp))
This prevents duplicate PRs for the same indicator across multiple scan windows.

